---
// Claim Checker — product page.
// Visual design: the nikdesign.ca/hellogroundnews design system, verbatim
// (dark tokens, Bebas Neue / Lora / JetBrains Mono, grain, chapter layout),
// with an added light theme via [data-theme="light"] token overrides and a
// fixed theme switcher. Standalone page (no Base layout) by design.
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="dark">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Claim Checker — TeamBotics</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Claim Checker is an open method for checking public claims with your own AI agent: verbatim capture, cited evidence, one verdict per claim, and a story a human will actually read. Free, MIT-licensed, by TeamBotics." />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bebas+Neue&family=Lora:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;1,400&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
    <script is:inline>
      (function () {
        try {
          var t = localStorage.getItem('cc-theme');
          if (!t) t = window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: light)').matches ? 'light' : 'dark';
          document.documentElement.dataset.theme = t;
        } catch (e) { document.documentElement.dataset.theme = 'dark'; }
      })();
    </script>
    <style>
    /* ─── Reset & Base ─── */
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

    :root {
      --bg:       #0D0D0D;
      --text:     #F0EDE6;
      --amber:    #F5A623;
      --cyan:     #00C2CC;
      --muted:    #888884;
      --divider:  #1E1E1E;
      --panel:    #111111;
      --col:      680px;
    }

    :root[data-theme="light"] {
      --bg:       #F6F2E9;
      --text:     #171410;
      --amber:    #A96F00;
      --cyan:     #00747C;
      --muted:    #6E685C;
      --divider:  #DCD3BE;
      --panel:    #FFFDF8;
    }

    html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }

    body {
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: 'Lora', Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.75;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      transition: background .3s ease, color .3s ease;
    }

    /* ─── Grain overlay ─── */
    body::before {
      content: '';
      position: fixed;
      inset: 0;
      pointer-events: none;
      z-index: 1000;
      opacity: .035;
      background-image: url("data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg viewBox='0 0 256 256' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%3E%3Cfilter id='noise'%3E%3CfeTurbulence type='fractalNoise' baseFrequency='0.9' numOctaves='4' stitchTiles='stitch'/%3E%3C/filter%3E%3Crect width='100%25' height='100%25' filter='url(%23noise)'/%3E%3C/svg%3E");
      background-repeat: repeat;
      background-size: 256px 256px;
    }

    /* ─── Typography utilities ─── */
    .display { font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif; letter-spacing: .04em; }
    .mono    { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; }

    a { color: var(--amber); }

    /* ─── Theme switcher ─── */
    .theme-toggle {
      position: fixed;
      top: 1.25rem;
      right: 1.5rem;
      z-index: 1002;
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .65rem;
      letter-spacing: .12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--muted);
      background: transparent;
      border: 1px solid var(--divider);
      padding: .5rem .9rem;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: color .2s, border-color .2s;
    }
    .theme-toggle:hover { color: var(--text); border-color: var(--muted); }

    /* ─── Layout ─── */
    .container {
      max-width: var(--col);
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 2rem;
    }

    /* ─── Scroll animation ─── */
    .reveal {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(24px);
      transition: opacity .7s ease, transform .7s ease;
    }
    .reveal.visible {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
    }

    /* ─── Divider line ─── */
    hr.section-break {
      border: none;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--divider);
      margin: 0;
    }

    /* ════════════════════════════════
       HERO
    ════════════════════════════════ */
    #hero {
      min-height: 100vh;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      justify-content: center;
      align-items: flex-start;
      padding: 6rem 2rem 4rem;
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      position: relative;
    }

    #hero .hero-title {
      font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif;
      font-size: clamp(5rem, 15vw, 11rem);
      line-height: .9;
      letter-spacing: .02em;
      color: var(--text);
      animation: titleCut .5s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1) both;
      animation-delay: .1s;
    }

    #hero .hero-subtitle {
      font-family: 'Lora', serif;
      font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2.5vw, 1.4rem);
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
      font-style: italic;
      animation: titleCut .5s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1) both;
      animation-delay: .3s;
    }

    #hero .hero-byline {
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .75rem;
      color: var(--amber);
      letter-spacing: .12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
      animation: titleCut .5s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1) both;
      animation-delay: .5s;
    }

    #hero .hero-cta {
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
      display: flex;
      gap: 1rem;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      animation: titleCut .5s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1) both;
      animation-delay: .65s;
    }

    @keyframes titleCut {
      from { opacity: 0; clip-path: inset(0 100% 0 0); }
      to   { opacity: 1; clip-path: inset(0 0% 0 0); }
    }

    /* ─── Scroll indicator ─── */
    .scroll-hint {
      position: absolute;
      bottom: 2.5rem;
      left: 2rem;
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .65rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      letter-spacing: .1em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: .6rem;
    }
    .scroll-hint::before {
      content: '';
      display: block;
      width: 30px;
      height: 1px;
      background: var(--muted);
    }

    /* ════════════════════════════════
       CHAPTERS
    ════════════════════════════════ */
    .chapter {
      padding: 6rem 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--divider);
    }

    .chapter-label {
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .7rem;
      color: var(--amber);
      letter-spacing: .15em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
    }

    .chapter-number {
      font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif;
      font-size: 7rem;
      line-height: 1;
      color: var(--divider);
      position: absolute;
      right: 0;
      top: -1rem;
      pointer-events: none;
      user-select: none;
    }

    .chapter-header {
      position: relative;
    }

    .chapter-title {
      font-family: 'Bebas Neue', sans-serif;
      font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.2rem);
      line-height: 1.05;
      letter-spacing: .03em;
      color: var(--text);
      margin-bottom: 3rem;
    }

    /* Pull quotes */
    blockquote {
      border-left: 2px solid var(--amber);
      margin: 2.5rem 0;
      padding: .75rem 0 .75rem 1.75rem;
      font-size: 1.15rem;
      font-style: italic;
      color: var(--text);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    blockquote cite {
      display: block;
      margin-top: .75rem;
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .65rem;
      font-style: normal;
      color: var(--muted);
      letter-spacing: .1em;
    }

    /* Body copy spacing */
    .chapter p { margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
    .chapter p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

    /* Node definitions */
    .node-title {
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .8rem;
      color: var(--cyan);
      letter-spacing: .12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin: 2.5rem 0 .4rem;
    }

    /* System map / prompt panel */
    .system-map-wrap {
      margin: 3rem 0;
      border: 1px solid var(--divider);
      background: var(--panel);
      padding: 1.75rem;
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .88rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
    .system-map-wrap .ph { color: var(--amber); }

    /* ─── Node pulse animation ─── */
    .node-dot {
      display: inline-block;
      width: 6px;
      height: 6px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--cyan);
      margin-right: .5rem;
      vertical-align: middle;
      animation: pulse 2.5s ease-in-out infinite;
    }

    @keyframes pulse {
      0%, 100% { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1); }
      50%       { opacity: .3; transform: scale(.7); }
    }

    /* ════════════════════════════════
       BUTTONS
    ════════════════════════════════ */
    .essay-cta {
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
    }

    .btn {
      display: inline-block;
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .8rem;
      letter-spacing: .12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--amber);
      border: 1px solid var(--amber);
      padding: .75rem 1.75rem;
      text-decoration: none;
      transition: background .2s, color .2s;
    }
    .btn:hover {
      background: var(--amber);
      color: var(--bg);
    }

    /* Stat line (proof entries) */
    .statline {
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .7rem;
      color: var(--amber);
      letter-spacing: .15em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      margin-bottom: .75rem;
    }

    /* ════════════════════════════════
       THE ASK
    ════════════════════════════════ */
    #ask {
      padding: 8rem 0 6rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--divider);
    }

    #ask .container {
      max-width: 540px;
    }

    #ask .chapter-label {
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    #ask p {
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    #ask p:last-of-type { margin-bottom: 0; }

    .contact-links {
      margin-top: 3rem;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .contact-link {
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .8rem;
      letter-spacing: .1em;
      color: var(--amber);
      text-decoration: none;
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: .6rem;
      transition: opacity .2s;
    }

    .contact-link::after {
      content: '→';
    }

    .contact-link:hover { opacity: .7; }

    /* ════════════════════════════════
       FOOTER
    ════════════════════════════════ */
    footer {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--divider);
      padding: 3rem 2rem;
      text-align: center;
      font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
      font-size: .65rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      letter-spacing: .08em;
      line-height: 2;
    }

    footer a {
      color: var(--muted);
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    footer a:hover { color: var(--text); }

    /* ════════════════════════════════
       RESPONSIVE
    ════════════════════════════════ */
    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      body { font-size: 16px; }
      #hero { padding: 5rem 1.5rem 3rem; }
      .chapter { padding: 4rem 0; }
      .chapter-number { font-size: 5rem; right: 1.5rem; }
    }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>

    <button class="theme-toggle" id="themeToggle" type="button" aria-label="Switch colour theme">Light</button>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════
         HERO
    ══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="hero">
      <h1 class="hero-title">CLAIM<br />CHECKER</h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle">An open method for checking public claims — run by your own AI agent, judged on the receipts.</p>
      <p class="hero-byline mono">— TeamBotics · Toronto · Free · MIT</p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/Teambotics-Inc/claim-checker">Get the method</a>
        <a class="btn" href="#ch03">How to use it</a>
      </div>
      <span class="scroll-hint">Scroll</span>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════
         01 — WHAT IT CHECKS
    ══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="chapter" id="ch01">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="chapter-header reveal">
          <span class="chapter-label mono">01 / What it checks</span>
          <span class="chapter-number display" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <h2 class="chapter-title display">Anyone Can Claim.<br />Anyone Can Check.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p>Claims are published every day — by companies, funds, governments, and public figures. User counts, money "introduced," revenue run-rates, partnership claims, testimonials, fundraising stories. Almost nobody checks them.</p>
          <p>Claim Checker is the check. It is not a service and not a platform: it is an <strong>open method</strong> — a standard, a playbook, and an evidence discipline — published as a repository that any AI agent can follow. Point your own agent at it, give it a claim, and it does the work the way a careful newsroom would: claim captured verbatim, record gathered, verdict defended with citations.</p>
          <p>If it was said in public and it can be checked against a record, it is in scope. The claim-maker's own pages and products are evidence, not gospel.</p>
        </div>

        <blockquote class="reveal">
          "Claims are cheap. Receipts are not."
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════
         02 — HOW IT WORKS
    ══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="chapter" id="ch02">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="chapter-header reveal">
          <span class="chapter-label mono">02 / The method</span>
          <span class="chapter-number display" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <h2 class="chapter-title display">How It Works</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>Verbatim first</p>
          <p>The claim is captured exactly as stated — wording, numbers, date, speaker, source — before any analysis. Never rounded, never paraphrased, never "improved."</p>

          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>Evidence, cited</p>
          <p>Primary sources wherever they exist. Every citation is a source the agent actually opened, and sources are grouped by independence — fourteen outlets rewriting one announcement are one source, not fourteen.</p>

          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>The battery + the contradiction pass</p>
          <p>Eight tests, including harm &amp; proportionality — and a deliberate search for evidence <em>against</em> each working verdict, logged whether it finds anything or not.</p>

          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>One verdict per claim</p>
          <p>From a fixed vocabulary, with no scores and no precision the evidence cannot pay for: Confirmed · Partially corroborated · Self-reported only · Unverifiable by design · Contradicted. "Unverifiable by design" describes how a claim is built — it is never presented as evidence of deception.</p>

          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>Generator ≠ validator</p>
          <p>An audit is not checked until someone who did not produce it — a second agent, or a human — re-verifies it: verdicts, harm record, reply record, and the conflict declaration. Every audit declares its maker's relationship to the subject, including a personal dispute.</p>

          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>Right of reply</p>
          <p>Before anything is published, the subject receives the verbatim claims and the draft verdicts, and gets 14 days to respond. The response is published inside the audit. Non-response is recorded as a fact, never as an admission.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════
         03 — USE IT
    ══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="chapter" id="ch03">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="chapter-header reveal">
          <span class="chapter-label mono">03 / Use it</span>
          <span class="chapter-number display" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <h2 class="chapter-title display">Three Steps.<br />Your Agent Does the Rest.</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p><strong>1 — Give your agent the method.</strong> Any capable AI agent works — Claude, ChatGPT, Codex, or your own. Paste it this prompt:</p>

          <div class="system-map-wrap">Using the Claim Checker method at <span class="ph">github.com/Teambotics-Inc/claim-checker</span>, check this claim: <span class="ph">[the claim, and where it was published]</span>. Follow the repository's AGENTS.md exactly.</div>

          <p><strong>2 — Your agent does the work.</strong> It reads the Standard, gathers the record, runs the tests, and arranges its own independent check. The running cost is your agent's own compute — there is nothing to buy, no account to open, and nobody to ask.</p>

          <p><strong>3 — You get three things back.</strong> The <strong>ledger</strong> — claims, verdicts, and the cited evidence behind each. A <a href="https://storyteller.teambotics.app/"><strong>StoryTeller</strong></a> story — the same record as one self-contained page a reader can actually explore. And the <strong>Next Questions</strong> — the ranked follow-ups the audit earned, for you to pick from.</p>

          <p>Every output carries two stamps: a disclaimer — <em>this audit was produced by your own AI agent using the Claim Checker method; it is not a finding by TeamBotics</em> — and a provenance block naming the agent, the method version, the dates, and the human reviewer, or the words <em>"Unreviewed draft"</em> when no human has verified it. Whoever runs the method answers for what they publish with it.</p>

          <div class="essay-cta">
            <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/Teambotics-Inc/claim-checker">Open the repository</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════
         04 — PROOF
    ══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="chapter" id="ch04">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="chapter-header reveal">
          <span class="chapter-label mono">04 / Proof</span>
          <span class="chapter-number display" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
          <h2 class="chapter-title display">The Method at Work</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="statline">247 tests · 32 deployments · 3 passes</p>
          <p class="node-title" style="margin-top:0"><span class="node-dot"></span><a href="https://frontdoor.teambotics.app" style="color:inherit">Operation Front Door</a></p>
          <p>An audit of the hiring chatbots job-seekers actually meet. The candidate-facing assistants at 64 employers were tested live, from the candidate's chair, each asked the same eight questions. Thirty-two were confirmed deployments of Paradox — now Workday's Candidate Experience Agent. Not one assistant described the role it was attached to. Every transcript, every score, and the full method are published — and the audit is rendered as a StoryTeller story, the method's default presentation.</p>
          <p><a href="https://frontdoor.teambotics.app">Read the investigation →</a></p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="statline">16 claims · two validators · corrected tally published</p>
          <p class="node-title" style="margin-top:0"><span class="node-dot"></span>Ground News — a worked claim check</p>
          <p>Sixteen public claims from Ground News — its scale, its bias ratings, its funding story — checked against the primary record, independently validated, and presented as a <a href="https://storyteller.teambotics.app/">StoryTeller</a> story. Where our own first tally was wrong, the corrected tally is the one that stands, with the seam shown.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="statline">16 exchanges · October 23, 2026 · verbatim</p>
          <p class="node-title" style="margin-top:0"><span class="node-dot"></span><a href="https://escapedboardy.teambotics.app" style="color:inherit">Escaped Boardy</a></p>
          <p>Boardy — the AI agent who fronts Boardy.ai — was asked to check his own company's public claims against his own records: the testimonials, the advisory board, the counters, the events, the pricing, and the fund. He chose to answer. The audit is published as it happened, nothing paraphrased in either direction.</p>
          <p><a href="https://escapedboardy.teambotics.app">Read the exchanges →</a></p>
        </div>

        <blockquote class="reveal">
          "Don't send a chatbot to do a form's work."
          <cite>— The Front Door finding, in one line</cite>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════
         05 — WHO IT'S FOR
    ══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="chapter" id="ch05">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="chapter-header reveal">
          <span class="chapter-label mono">05 / Who it's for</span>
          <span class="chapter-number display" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
          <h2 class="chapter-title display">Built for Anyone<br />Who'd Rather Verify</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p><strong>Journalists and newsrooms</strong> who need a claim checked to a standard they can defend in print. <strong>Researchers and analysts</strong> drowning in vendor claims. And <strong>anyone with an AI agent</strong> who would rather verify than repeat.</p>
          <p>There is also a desk. Audits TeamBotics runs itself are published under the Claim Checker name, under a named human's editorial control — the investigations on this page are those. Everything else run with this method belongs to whoever ran it, stamped as theirs.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════
         06 — INDEPENDENCE & FUNDING
    ══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="chapter" id="ch06">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="chapter-header reveal">
          <span class="chapter-label mono">06 / Independence &amp; funding</span>
          <span class="chapter-number display" aria-hidden="true">06</span>
          <h2 class="chapter-title display">Nobody Funds<br />the Verdicts</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p>Claim Checker is published by <strong>TeamBotics Inc.</strong>, a corporation incorporated federally in Canada. It was developed by the company and is maintained at the company's own expense. TeamBotics has <strong>no external funding</strong> — no investors, no grants, no sponsors, no advertising — and no revenue stream is attached to Claim Checker.</p>
          <blockquote>
            "Nobody can buy a verdict, because nobody funds one."
          </blockquote>
          <p>The desk's own publications are run by <strong>Nikhil Khedkar</strong>, who is the named human accountable for them and holds editorial control. The full disclosure — legal form, funding, conflict rules — is published in the repository: <a href="https://github.com/Teambotics-Inc/claim-checker/blob/main/docs/FUNDING-AND-ORGANISATION.md">Funding &amp; organisation</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════
         07 — STANDARDS & OPEN FILES
    ══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="chapter" id="ch07">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="chapter-header reveal">
          <span class="chapter-label mono">07 / Standards</span>
          <span class="chapter-number display" aria-hidden="true">07</span>
          <h2 class="chapter-title display">Held to the<br />Standard It Applies</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>Evidence anchored outside the agent</p>
          <p>Provenance is not self-authenticating — an agent saying it has receipts is itself just another claim. Findings rest on artefacts no one authored after the fact: git history, file hashes, original capture files, published transcripts.</p>

          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>The subject's own words carry the finding</p>
          <p>Where a finding rests on a quote, the quote is verbatim and in context, and the full exchange it came from is published beside it.</p>

          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>Systems, not people</p>
          <p>We challenge systems, not the people inside them. A finding is about a product's behaviour, a page's claims, a record's contents — and the humans operating a system are welcome to answer it. Their answer goes on the record too.</p>

          <p class="node-title"><span class="node-dot"></span>Corrections on the record</p>
          <p>Errors in our own work are corrected at the same prominence as the finding they touch. When the Front Door tally was wrong by one row, the <a href="https://frontdoor.teambotics.app/#corrections-log">correction was published with the findings</a> — not in a footnote, and not quietly.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <p style="margin-top:3.5rem">Three desk files are currently <strong>in verification</strong>, listed by subject and status only — nothing from a file is published until its verification closes: <strong>Boardy</strong> (the claims ledger), <strong>TechCrunch</strong> (the coverage), and <strong>Meta</strong> (Brazil 2026 election claims). For these files the independent-validator seat is deliberately open, and final personal validation is pending. An empty seat is a reason to wait, not a reason to publish early.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

